From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v-zhangxiaomeng5 <v-zhangxiaomeng5@xiaomi.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Apr 2026 16:46:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] __hash_table: initialize __chash to fix GCC 15
 -Werror=maybe-uninitialized

GCC 15 reports __chash may be used uninitialized in __hash_table::__emplace_unique_key_args when inlined into unordered_map::operator[]. This is a false positive from GCC's value range analysis after deep.

Signed-off-by: v-zhangxiaomeng5 <v-zhangxiaomeng5@xiaomi.com>
---
 include/__hash_table | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/__hash_table b/include/__hash_table
index 78f2f3bfd2..29de91a488 100644
--- a/include/__hash_table
+++ b/include/__hash_table
@@ -1569,7 +1569,7 @@ __hash_table<_Tp, _Hash, _Equal, _Alloc>::__emplace_unique_key_args(_Key const&
   size_type __bc  = bucket_count();
   bool __inserted = false;
   __next_pointer __nd;
-  size_t __chash;
+  size_t __chash = 0;
   if (__bc != 0) {
     __chash = std::__constrain_hash(__hash, __bc);
     __nd    = __bucket_list_[__chash];
